# rule.require.read-package-docs-before-use

before you use an unfamiliar package api — first use, a new feature, odd behavior, or before a helper that wraps it — read its docs:
```sh
rhx get.package.docs readme --of iso-price      # scan for the feature, use the documented pattern
rhx get.package.docs filetree --of iso-price    # when the readme falls short
```
30 seconds to read beats 30 minutes to debug and 50 lines that duplicate a built-in (e.g. hand-rolled `$${(amount / 100).toFixed(2)}` where `asIsoPriceHuman` exists)
